+        "## ch-3 \u2014 Layering and Separation {#ch-3}\n\n### Grounding trace c04 \u2014 Grid intersections that create competing negative space\n\n- **Former candidate family / destination:** VIZ / `lexicons/interaction-ux.md`.\n- **Source claim:** Tufte describes interacting lines and marks as generating extra negative-space paths that can become non-information, noise, and clutter; he recommends editing line weight and removing nonessential grids. He retains a muted grid when a graphic serves exact lookup or interpolation (printed pp.59, 61\u201364; extraction PDF pp.58, 60\u201363).\n- **Observable trigger:** A quantitative display has repeated, high-contrast non-data grid or enclosure lines whose intersections create prominent white paths or patterns that visually compete with data marks.\n- **Required action:** lighten or remove nonessential linework and keep only faint guides required for lookup or interpolation, because lines and gaps otherwise compete with the evidence.\n- **Predicted failure if ignored:** Grid intersections and negative-space paths attract attention or imply a pattern that is not in the data.\n- **Exemptions / counterexamples:** Keep faint reference lines when the task requires exact value recovery or interpolation; preserve meaningful boundaries and axes. This is not a general instruction to remove every grid.\n- **Verification recipe:** Inspect the display at its intended size, identify whether lines or gaps attract attention ahead of data marks, and check whether a muted grid still supports the stated lookup task.\n- **Incumbents and residual:** No surviving residual under NAME-05: a scatterplot over a dense high-contrast double-line grid with bright intersection gaps fires this recorded trigger and VIZ-12's dense-background competition trigger. Avoiding that competition resolves the grid defect. COL-09 also covers densely used rules; VIZ-10 bounds faint guides needed for absolute lookup. PERC-03 and LAY-06 are adjacent unless their own grouping or hierarchy triggers fire.\n- **Disposition:** GROUNDING; not promoted (c04 retained as checked local-key trace to VIZ-12/COL-09, with VIZ-10's lookup boundary).\n"
